==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ballet Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Curry Cat''' when obtained from [[Revenge of the Wormhole (Merciless)|Revenge of the Wormhole]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Volley Cat is a very effective [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal Cat]], due to her long range and surprisingly high [[Critical Hit]] damage. However, her blind spot renders her useless against close-ranged [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal enemies]] such as [[Metal One Horn]] and [[Super Metal Hippoe]] if they aren't kept within her range.

Overall, Volley Cat is a great addition to most anti-Metal lineups as her long range and fast attack rate make for a reliable [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] if properly meatshielded. It is recommended to use something like [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] or [[Rope Jump Cat (Rare Cat)|Noodle Cats]] to cover her blind spot.

It's worth noting that her niche as a ranged Critter becomes significantly less important once [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] is acquired, who can do the same thing but with more reliability and range in exchange for some damage.

==='''True Form'''===
Curry Cat's 100% slow combined with high attack rate and low cooldown makes for a great combination. The blind spot still remains an issue, but could allow it to halt the progress of Metal enemies that are approaching. However, the brief slow can also interrupt the slow of other units such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]] or [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster & Charley]]. Despite the potential for overriding other units' slow, Curry Cat is still overall a great improvement when compared to his previous forms.

